 only with keratin immunohistochemistry  spanning  0 02cm   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  2 Number of lymph nodes examined  9 Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  2  largest focus spans 0 1cm    Size of largest lymph node  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL INFERIOR   EXCISION INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  PRESENT AT THE MARGIN  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL MEDIAL   EXCISION  INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left lumpectomy breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch indicating anterior and a long stitch indicating lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic area possibly representing a previous biopsy site  0 1cm from the posterior margin  0 5cm from the superior margin  0 5cm from the anterior margin  1 4cm from the inferior margin and 1 0cm from the medial and lateral margins  The remainder of the specimen is fibrofatty and partially rubbery with no other lesions or masses identified  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the hemorrhagic area with closest posterior and superior margins  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and   left axillary lymph nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of cauterized fatty tissue containing 4 grossly identified lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The largest lymph node is bivalved and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining 3 nodes are entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the tissue is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast additional inferior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm breast tissue oriented by a stitch indicating the new margin  The latter is inked black  Entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast additional medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented breast tissue which is entirely submitted in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Norma Rodriguez M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Norma Rodriguez M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Norma Rodriguez M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum note  An immunohistochemical stain for E cadherin shows strong positive staining of the invasive carcinoma  This result supports infiltrating ductal carcinoma rather than infiltrating lobular carcinoma  Addendum  2 by Kristina Br