OCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND CALCIFICATIONS  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH RADIATION TREATMENT EFFECT  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  NOTE  The focus of low grade ductal carcinoma in situ in the current specimen was compared with the foci in the patient s previous excision   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and found to be morphologically similar  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptors on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a long stitch denoting lateral and a short stitch denoting posterior  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm of attached  elliptical tan skin which has a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm everted nipple  There is a 4 0cm in length scar that is 3 4cm from the nipple  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior margin inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white  glistening fibrous area that is consistent with a well healed previous biopsy cavity  The fibrous area is directly sub adjacent to the scar  is 1 5cm from the posterior margin and 0 4cm from the nearest anterior soft tissue margin  The remaining breast tissue is predominantly tan yellow unremarkable adipose tissue  No other masses or lesions are identified  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest deep margin to previous biopsy site   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire previous biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from central region  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating superior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan elliptical portion of attached skin with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm everted nipple  The skin surface shows a 2 0cm in length well healed scar that is 4 0cm from the nipple  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm exposed previous biopsy cavity along the most medial aspect which communicates with the posterior  and anterior soft tissue margins  The exposed lining of the biopsy cavity is tan pink  fibrotic and focally hemorrhagic  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior aspect is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial  The remaining breast tissue is predominantly tan yellow unremarkable adipose tissue  No other masses or lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from lower outer quadrant  Gross Dictation by Heather Burton  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Christine Garcia M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachuse