Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 19 11 CLINICAL DATA  History of infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the right breast measuring 1 7cm  on a biopsy from an outside hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The residual tumor is present around the old biopsy cavity with the largest focus measuring 0 5cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  The tumor is present on the inked border of the inferior en face resection margin and extends to within 0 2cm of the anterior  0 1cm of the deep  0 3cm of the lateral and 0 3cm of the medial margins  2  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  3  GRANULATION TISSUE  FAT NECROSIS  AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION CONSISTENT WITH RECENT BIOPSY CAVITY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  TWO OF 16 LYMPH NODES ARE POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 39                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  in three separate parts  Labeled  right breast  short superior  long lateral  is a 76 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  breast lumpectomy specimen with an overlying 4 7cm  long and REMOVED_DATE wide skin ellipse that contains a centrally located  longitudinal  4 2cm  long  well healed scar  A short suture designates the superior margin  and a long suture designates the lateral margin  The specimen is inked in black entirely  and then double inked in blue on the anterior surface  red on the lateral surface  and yellow on the medial surface  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  hemorrhagic  oval biopsy cavity that is located 0 5cm  from the nearest medial margin  0 8cm  from the lateral margin  1 2cm  from the superior margin  1 2cm  from the inferior margin  0 3cm  from the deep margin  and 1 2cm  from the skin or anterior surface  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by focally white  shiny  rubbery breast tissue and scattered  irregular  bright yellow areas  that extend focally to all of the resection margins  Labeled  axillary node  is a 11 x 6 x 2cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal multiple  16  lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are bisected to reveal a tan to brown to fatty cut surface  One half of each is submitted  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  are multiple portions of fibroadipose tissue measuring 4 x 5 x 2 5cm  in aggregate  The specimen is dissected to reveal multiple  5  lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1cm  in greatest dimension  and having a tan to freshly pink cut surface  One half of each is submitted  Section code  A  Superior resection margin  en face  B  Inferior resection margin  en face  C  Medial resection margin and biopsy cavity  radial section  D  Lateral resection margin and biopsy cavity  radial section  E  Deep resection margin and biopsy cavity  radial section  F  Skin with biopsy cavity  G Q  Biopsy cavity  representative sections  R S  Breast parenchyma  representative sections  T AA  Axillary lymph nodes  one  half of each  AB AC  Additional axillary lymph nodes  one half of each  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Katherine Keeley  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  PART B  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA  PART C  BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
