ng of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 94 at 07 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 5 x 3 x 1cm tan  red fibrofatty tissue with a needle wire and x ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular ill defined stellate mass 0 3cm from the closest inked margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through I  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS FOR MALIGNANCY  TOO SMALL FOR FROZEN SECTION  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  Janey Pratt  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
