 determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm attached axilla and he overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm white tan skin and 4 0cm nipple  There is a 5 0cm well healed scar 4 0cm lateral to the nipple and a 4 5cm well healed scar 10 5cm lateral to the nipple  Specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cavity with a brown tan surface  Adjacent to the cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white firm area  The cavity is 2 5cm from the inked deep margin  The area of white firm nodularity is anterior to the cavity and comes to within 1 1cm of the skin surface  A metal clip is found in the white tan nodule adjacent to the cavity  Additionally  around the cavity there are foci of yellow tan fatty necrosis  There are focal areas of white breast parenchyma with palpable small nodularity  The remainder of the parenchyma is yellow tan with unremarkable white breast parenchyma  Within the axilla  multiple lymph nodes ranging from 0 2cm in diameter to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm are identified  Numerous lymph nodes are bisected to reveal a white tan cut surface with focal areas of hemorrhage  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  margin closest to cavity B G  cavity and adjacent white tan tissue  cassettes E F contain white tan tissue in cavity adjacent to metal clip  H  white tan tissue and focal areas of hemorrhage I  white tan breast parenchyma with focal nodularity J O  bisected palpable nodes P  probable smaller nodes submitted entirely  Resident  CHAD SOUPIR  MD                                                                                 SOU