d to reveal several firm  tan nodules  The largest nodule is 0 6cm in diameter  Representative of each is submitted in cassettes L through O  Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST RE EXCISION PART B  LEFT AXILLARY NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 15 29 CLINICAL DATA  Left core biopsy showed invasive carcinoma  Now also with medial calcifications in the lumpectomy specimen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  SEE TABLE 1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH NECROSIS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Multiple independent foci of invasive tumor are present  ranging from 1 9cm in the lateral breast  site of localization wires    0 9cm in the medial breast  site of additional localization wires   to several smaller independent foci scattered between these largest areas of invasion  Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The dominant area of invasive tumor in the lateral portion of the specimen is focally positive at the inferior margin and extends to less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus  Another focus of invasive tumor in the medial portion of the specimen focally approaches within 0 1cm of the anterior margin  An additional microfocus of invasive tumor in the medial specimen is within 0 2cm of the superior margin  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on block E  LYMPH NODE  LEFT   PRIMARY  AXILLA SENTINEL   BIOPSY  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE NOTE  The metastatic deposit  1cm   replaces the node and extends into the extranodal adipose extensively  LYMPH NODE  LEFT   SECONDARY  AXILLA SENTINEL   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  LEFT   TERTIARY   AXILLA SENTINEL   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16 36                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block E   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 15 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x 9 x 3 7cm fragment of fibrofatty breast parenchyma with four needle localization wires  two in the medial portion of the specimen and two in the lateral portion of the specimen  A bow tie designates the cephalad margin  a short suture denotes the inferior margin  and a long suture denotes the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  and inferior   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan white  stellate  and firm region in the lateral portion of the specimen  2 5cm from the lateral margin  0 9cm from the anterior margin  0 6cm from the inferior margin  5 0cm from the superior margin  and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  This area is in the region of two of the needle localization wires  Also noted in the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm region denoted by two needle localization wires in the medial portion of the specimen which show a focally calcified and fibrotic region  Also within this region  there are focal small  round  tan yellow areas which appear to represent caseous necrosis  There is no distinct mass identified  The intervening breast parenchyma is tan white  focally fibrous  and predominant fibrofatty  Photographs of the specimen have been taken  Representative sections are submitted as per section code  Section Code  A D  0 9cm nodule in lateral breast  E G  Intervening unremarkable appearing breast parenchyma  H P  Calcifications denoted by medial localization wires  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  primary sentinel node  150   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm node  In addition  a smaller firm region of possibly hemorrhagic fat is noted in the specimen  The largest lymph node is bisected to reveal a tan white and focally fatty cut surface with scattered punctate red foci  This largest bisected node is entirely submitted into cassette Q  the remainder fibrofatty tissue and smaller nodular region are submitted into cassette R  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  secondary sentinel node  80   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggegrate of yellow fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node  The lymph node and attached fibrofatty tissue are entirely submitted into cassette S  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  tertiary sentinel node  79   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm lymph node with a fibrofatty and focally tan pink cut surface  The bisected node is entirely submitted into cassette T and U and the remainder of the fibrofatty tissue is entirely submitted into cassette V  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE LEFT PRIMARY AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE LEFT SECONDARY AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISIO PART D  LYMPH NODE LEFT TERTIARY AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISION , Unchecked.
