gments of tan  yellow  firm  irregular  fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in aggregate  Multiple lymph nodes are ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm dissected and placed in V X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Additional lateral tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm yellow tan  fibrofatty  irregular shaped piece of tissue  Specimen is sectioned to reveal a yellow  lobulated  fibrofatty cut surface  Specimen is submitted in entirety in cassette Y BB  Section code  A  Posterior margin B  Anterior margin C  Superior margin D H  Upper outer quadrant representative sections of mass I  Representative sections from left inner quadrant J  Representative sections from upper inner quadrant K  Representative sections from lower outer quadrant L X  Lymph node Y BB  Additional lateral tissue  CC HH  Additional sections of mass from main specimen The axillary tail is removed from the main breast specimen and multiple lymph nodes are dissected out and submitted in cassettes L through U  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  are multiple fragments of tan yellow  firm  irregular  fibrofatty pieces of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm in aggregate  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected and placed in V through X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm yellow tan  fibrofatty  irregular shaved piece of tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a yellow  lobulated  fibrofatty cut surface  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes Y through BB  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     O R  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPA