mpared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm skin ellipse containing a nipple and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The posterior deep resection margin is inked black  the superior anterior surface is inked blue  and the inferior anterior surface is inked green  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm stellate shaped rubbery mass with ill defined border  containing a 1 0cm diameter biopsy cavity  The mass extends to within 0 4cm from the deep resection margin  A second focus of scar is located approximately 1 5cm superior to the main biopsy cavity and about 1 0cm from the anterior  and 1 0cm from the posterior resection margin  The rest of the specimen consists of yellow  focally white breast parenchyma with focal cystic area up to 0 2cm in diameter  Dissection of the axillary tail reveals multliple lymph nodes up to 2 0cm in diameter  Section Code  A  mass at the closest margin  deep  B  second scar superior to the first biopsy cavity C D  and E  representative section of the mass around the first biopsy cavity F  tissue around the second  superio r scar N G  1 0cm diameter firm area at the anterior inferior margin  9 0cm inferior from the center of the first biopsy cavity  Q H  breast parenchyma with focal cysts I L  axillary lymph nodes  O P  breast parenchyma with dilated ducts containing white to yellow soft contents  Received within the same container within a specimen cup  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number with no further specification  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in M  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  AND AXILLARY TAIL PART B  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
