  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a tan  yellow  irregular 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of breast tissue infiltrated with blue dye  The specimen is inked black  The posterior is overinked blue  the superior is overinked with yellow and sectioned to reveal a stellate 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm mass that focally abuts the posterior margin  SECTION CODE A D  Tumor  with  almost entirely submitted  closest margins in A and B  E F  Representative sections of breast not involving tumor  Also received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm piece of yellow tan tissue which is bisected and totally submitted in G  Also received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  2  is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of yellow tan firm lymph node which is bisected and totally submitted in H  