entric  disease  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla sentinel node   is a soft tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  which was previously bisected and appears consistent with a lymph node  The lymph node is now entirely frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right simple mastectomy with a short stitch designating 12 o clock  The anterior aspect is inked blue  and the posterior aspect of the specimen is inked black  The overlying 4 3cm tan skin ellipse contains a 3 x 3cm nipple   areola complex with an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE nipple  No scars are identified  In the same container  there are also two unoriented breast tissue fragments which are fatty and measure REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm respectively  Both unoriented fatty fragments are inked in black  serially sectioned  and appear grossly unremarkable  The main specimen is serially sectioned along the medial   lateral long axis and four firm white tumor masses are identified  The tumor mass  1 is located approximately at 5 o clock  under the nipple areola complex area  and measures 0 6cm in largest dimension  It is 0 2cm from the posterior resection margin  1cm from the anterior resection margin  5 5cm from the nipple areola complex  1cm from tumor mass  2  and 6cm from the tumor mass  4  The 2nd tumor mass is also at approximately 5 o clock and is 4 x 3 x 1 8cm  1 5cm from the nipple areola complex  0 1cm from the posterior resection margin  and 0 5cm from the anterior resection margin  The tumor mass  3 is 0 7cm in greatest dimension  is approximately at 6 o clock  3cm from the anterior resection margin  1cm from the posterior resection margin  and 0 8cm from the tumor mass  2  The tumor mass  4 is approximately at 10 o clock  and it measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and it is 2cm from the posterior resection margin  and 2 5cm from the anterior resection margin  The tumor mass  4 is rubbery and well circumscribed  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly multifibrotic  No other lesions are grossly identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor mass  1  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma between tumor mass  1 and tumor mass  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the tumor mass  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor mass  3  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma between tumor mass  2 and tumor mass  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor mass  4  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma between tumor mass  2 and  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma away from the masses  medially  at 3cm from the larger tumor mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma away from the tumor masses  at 3 5cm from the larger one  laterally   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five representative sections of tissue near the axillary region  query axillary nodes   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right mastectomy flap   are four unoriented fragments of skin measuring 13 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 6cm  and REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm respectively  All four fragmented skin specimens appear grossly unremarkable  A representative section of each of them is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  F