Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 32 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MASS   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 1  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL   ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SMALL FOCUS  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   6 O CLOCK    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  It is difficult to determine the size of the tumor present in the specimen labeled  6 o clock   Carcinoma is present in 4 of the 6 blocks  and the largest focus spans 0 5cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen in any specimen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   MASS    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm ill defined white tan  stellate firm nodule  abutting the inked margin  A section of the nodule is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in A  The remaining nodule and neighboring tissue are submitted in B E  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Medial breast mass  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal white fibrous tissue with no suspicious lesions  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes F through I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Lateral breast mass  right side  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast inked and sectioned to reveal tan yellow moderately firm tissue  grossly abutting the inked surface  submitted entirely in cassettes J through N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  6 o clock  