e  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  16 MAY 02 at 12 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan brown lymph node with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fat  The fat is removed and the lymph node is entirely frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch denoting the superior aspect  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 9 5cm skin ellipse with a 1 0cm nipple and a 3 5cm unremarkable areola area and a 3 5cm unremarkable areolar area  There appear to be two punctate scars at the 10 and 12 0 clock positions located 2 0cm from the nipple  Also remarkable are REMOVED_DATE verrucous lesions measuring REMOVED_DATE and 0 8cm in greatest dimension  located REMOVED_DATE and 6 5cm lateral from the nipple  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a hard ill circumscribed white mass with a gritty cut surface measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and located 0 6cm from the deep posterior margin  appearing to grossly abut the anterior skin surface  located 3 5cm from the superior aspect of the specimen  and a 3 0cm from the medial aspect of the specimen  The remaining parenchyma is composed of unremarkable fibrofatty tissue without nodules  masses or gross calcifications noted  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  B  mass and black inked posterior margin  C  mass with anterior skin taken at nipple  D E  additional sections of mass  F  unremarkable parenchyma at superior aspect of the specimen  G I  blue tinged parenchyma in area adjacent to mass  J  additional sections of mass  K L  lymph node candidates  Resident  CHRISTINE GARCIA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  ARASH RADFAR  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  , Checked.
