e is an exposed cavity along the anterior aspect  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy site  contiguous with the one exposed to the anterior aspect  The cavity lining is tan pink  smooth glistening and fibrotic with focal areas of fat necrosis  The cavity comes to 0 3cm from the posterior  0 5cm from the superior  0 9cm from the inferior  0 4cm from the lateral and 0 2cm from the medial margins  respectively  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow pink  lobulated and unremarkable  Representative sections of the cavity are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the medial margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast superior medial margin cyst at through outside margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular tan yellow pink fibrofatty tissue with a suture along one aspect designating the true outside margin  The stitched aspect is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a unremarkable fibrofatty cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 3  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES  CFG AER Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Shabin Nanji M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  SENTINEL NODE  LEFT AXILLARY   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
