Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  1 3cm  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN 0 1cm OF MULTIPLE MARGINS  WITH LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  IN THE REGION OF AND JUST BEYOND THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  ASSOCIATED WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number and  right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm fragment of breast with wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  round  firm nodule with focal gritty  white areas present at the inked resection margin  A piece is frozen as FX 1  then submitted in cassette F  The remaining is submitted in cassettes A through B  A rubbery well demarcated white fibrous area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 2cm  submitted in part in cassette C through D  Representative sections of normal breast is submitted in cassette E  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
