Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 18 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  enchancing area on the left on MRI                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA SCATTERED FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 4 x 3 x 1cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal diffuse fibrocystic changes throughout the specimen without any areas grossly suspicious for carcinoma  Entirely submitted in A through I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left additional and final margin  is a 2 x 4 x 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue inked black and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Submitted entirely in J through T  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION   NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
