h certainty if this focus  represents ductal carcinoma in situ or invasive carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Immunostains  for p63 and myosin were evaluated   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID         GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a 23 x  16 x 2cm mastectomy specimen  with attached REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm piece of axillary  tissue  with a suture designating the axillary tail  The overlying 15 x 5 5cm  ellipse of skin appears unremarkable  The nipple and areola appear  unremarkable  The anterior margin is inked blue  and posterior margin is inked  black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan pink  firm   well circumscribed mass  located in the subareolar region  which extends to 2  cm from posterior margin and 1 5cm from anterior margin  Adjacent and  abutting the main nodule at its inferior pole  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  tan brown  fairly well circumscribed nodule  which extends to 2 5cm from  anterior and 4cm from posterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma  contains predominantly tan yellow lobulated interspersed with minimal amount of  tan white fibrous tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected  ranging in size  from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The following sections are  submitted      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of main mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  submitted in formalin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   submitted in Penfix    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of main mass and entire adjacent smaller nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma  upper outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma  inner lower quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 whole lymph nodes per cassette    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 whole lymph node    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibroadipose tissue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   S