S FOLLOWS  REMOVED_DATE CM IN THE FIRST NODE WITH REMOVED_DATE CM ADJACENT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  TOGETHER SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM   THE SECOND SENTINEL NODE CONTAINS REMOVED_DATE CM TUMOR WITH REMOVED_DATE CM ADJACENT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  TOGETHER SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM   THE AXILLARY CONTENTS CONTAIN REMOVED_DATE POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  THE TUMOR IS PRESENT IN THE FORM OF 2 SMALL DEPOSITS IN THE SUBCAPSULAR SINUS  ONE COMPOSED OF 20 CELLS  THE OTHER OF 15 CELLS   ONE IN EACH HALF OF THE BISECTED NODE  THEREFORE MAY REPRESENT THE SAME FOCUS  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 08 49     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Right Axillary  Sentinel   block B   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 14 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fibroadipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node  The specimen is bisected  entirely submitted in cassettes A B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast needle localization  is a 5 x 4 x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose breast tissue  A short stitch indicates superior  long stitch lateral  as designated by the surgeon  The specimen is oriented  inked black on the posterior surface  blue anterior  Sectioning reveals an ill defined  firm white fibrous nodule of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm in greatest dimension in the superior lateral portion of the specimen  abutting the posterior  black  margin  Ill defined  firm  vaguely lobular fibrous strands are present throughout the specimen  with no further discrete lesion identified  The fibrous tissue occupies 40  of the specimen  the remainder consists of lobular adipose tissue with focal hemorrhage  0 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in the superior portion of the specimen   SECTION CODE C H  Serial sections  superior portion of specimen with hard nodule in C  a 0 5cm metal ring removed from section in cassette E and focal hemorrhage in cassettes E F  Sections are submitted from lateral to medial I O  Inferior portion of the specimen  serial sections from lateral to medial  The specimen is entirely submitted Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x 7 x 3cm fibroadipose tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are identified and submitted in cassettes P Y  Cassette T contains two bisected nodes  W X contain one bisected node each Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
