gin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Note  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the myoepithelial layer in areas of ductal carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  Immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is negative in areas of lobular carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  The areas of LCIS are intermixed with the DCIS  The LCIS involves areas of sclerosing adenosis and a fibroadenoma and extends to all margins of resection in the specimen  C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION 1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MICROSCOPIC FOCI 2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS GREATER THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN OF RESECTION  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  NOTE  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is negative in areas of lobular carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  Multiple level sections were evaluated  D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION 1  EXTENSIVE LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MILD USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   are negative in areas of lobular carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  Immunohistochemical stains for keratin REMOVED_DATE performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlight luminal ductal cells in